  "adaptation": {
    "semantic": "The number, the replacing pronoun (a red one), and the formal general pronoun (one should) are three different words in most languages. The replacing use has no equivalent in many, which repeat the noun or use the adjective alone.",
    "grammar": "One takes a singular noun and verb: one child is. After one of, the noun is plural and the verb singular: one of the children is here. The replacing one follows an adjective, this, that, which, or the, and has a plural, ones.",
    "culture": null,
    "false_friends": null,
    "pronunciation": "Pronounced wʌn, exactly like won, with the vowel of sun; the spelling with o misleads. The w sound is not written."
  },
